":true,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/language/LanguageAdvancedRecords.json","corpus":"language","recordShard":36,"revisionDate":"12 October 2026","markdown":"## adv-rashii-typical : らしい : conforme à ce qui caractérise (12 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N3 ; statut : editorial-draft. (12 October 2026)\n\nNom + らしい peut décrire une caractéristique attendue ou typique de ce nom. Cet emploi se conjugue comme un adjectif en い et forme aussi らしさ. (12 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| 春らしい天気ですね。 (はるらしいてんきですね。) | C’est un temps bien printanier. (12 October 2026) |\n| 自分らしく話してください。 (じぶんらしくはなしてください。) | Exprimez-vous à votre manière. (12 October 2026) |\n| この町らしい景色です。 (このまちらしいけしきです。) | Ce paysage est caractéristique de cette ville. (12 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-verb-groups, grammar-copula. (12 October 2026)\n\n- [The Auxiliary ～らしい](https://imabi.org/the-auxiliary-%ef%bd%9e%e3%82%89%e3%81%97%e3%81%84/) ; Seth Coonrod, original IMABI curriculum author ; Copyright retained by author; no open license verified ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (12 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"eccce71ba05578d788a31e882edea14449c9cac5fdaf9fcf6a3c4020489d8065","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"eccce71ba05578d788a31e882edea14449c9cac5fdaf9fcf6a3c4020489d8065","reviewerIds":["/root/language_review_a","/root/language_review_b"],"evidenceUrls":["https://imabi.org/the-auxiliary-%ef%bd%9e%e3%82%89%e3%81%97%e3%81%84/"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtByReviewer":{"/root/language_review_a":null,"/root/language_review_b":"13 October 2026"},"reviewType":"independent-adversarial-model-review","humanReview":false}},{"id":"adv-souda-appearance","title":"そうだ : une apparence perceptible","domain":"grammar","level":"N4","levelBasis":"Editorial difficulty estimate; not an official JLPT item assignment","taxonomy":"evidence","aliases":["souda-appearance","そうだ"],"explanationFr":"Base de ます + そうだ annonce une apparence ou une imminence. Un adjectif en い perd い ; un adjectif en な se rattache sans な. いい donne よさそう ; l’adjectif ない donne なさそう. Ces règles ne se transposent pas sans contrôle à toutes les négations verbales.","contrastFr":"おいしそう signifie « semble bon » ; おいしいそう rapporte une information reçue. かわいそう signifie « qui fait pitié », pas « semble mignon » ; pour ce dernier sens, employer かわいいようだ.","examples":[{"ja":"この料理はおいしそうです。","reading":"このりょうりはおいしそうです。","fr":"Ce plat a l’air bon.","origin":"Original example, independent native review pending"},{"ja":"雨が降りそうです。","reading":"あめがふりそうです。","fr":"Il semble qu’il va pleuvoir.","origin":"Original example, independent native review pending"},{"ja":"この方法はよさそうです。","reading":"このほうほうはよさそうです。","fr":"Cette méthode semble bonne.","origin":"Original example, independent native review pending"}],"prerequisites":["grammar-relative-clause","grammar-verb-groups"],"sources":[{"url":"https://imabi.org/seem-%ef%bd%9e%e3%81%9d%e3%81%86%e3%81%a0/","title":"Seem: ～そうだ","publisher":"Seth Coonrod, original IMABI curriculum author","checkedAt":"12 October 2026","availability":"fetched","verification":"Source fetched; pedagogical source alignment reviewed editorially; no native review claimed","license":"Copyright retained by author; no open license verified","reuse":"Original paraphrase and examples; source lessons, recordings and illustrations not reproduced"}],"status":"editorial-draft","reviewScope":"Editorial linguistic review only; native-speaker review and learner testing pending","createdAt":"12 October 2026","learnerState":"not-assessed","oralPromptsFr":["Ce plat a l’air bon.","Il semble qu’il va pleuvoir.","Cette méthode semble bonne."],"levelEstimated":true,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/language/LanguageAdvancedRecords.json","corpus":"language","recordShard":250,"revisionDate":"13 October 2026","markdown":"## adv-souda-appearance : そうだ : une apparence perceptible (13 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N4 ; statut : editorial-draft. (13 October 2026)\n\nBase de ます + そうだ annonce une apparence ou une imminence. Un adjectif en い perd い ; un adjectif en な se rattache sans な. いい donne よさそう ; l’adjectif ない donne なさそう. Ces règles ne se transposent pas sans contrôle à toutes les négations verbales. (13 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| この料理はおいしそうです。 (このりょうりはおいしそうです。) | Ce plat a l’air bon. (13 October 2026) |\n| 雨が降りそうです。 (あめがふりそうです。) | Il semble qu’il va pleuvoir. (13 October 2026) |\n| この方法はよさそうです。 (このほうほうはよさそうです。) | Cette méthode semble bonne. (13 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-relative-clause, grammar-verb-groups. (13 October 2026)\n\n- [Seem: ～そうだ](https://imabi.org/seem-%ef%bd%9e%e3%81%9d%e3%81%86%e3%81%a0/) ; Seth Coonrod, original IMABI curriculum author ; Copyright retained by author; no open license verified ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (13 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"7c0d62569dc15740394b57704dc87f5f926d3902de51b1114a19f23f5f01b570","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"7c0d62569dc15740394b57704dc87f5f926d3902de51b1114a19f23f5f01b570","reviewerIds":["/root/language_review_a","/root/language_review_b"],"evidenceUrls":["https://imabi.org/seem-%ef%bd%9e%e3%81%9d%e3%81%86%e3%81%a0/"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtByReviewer":{"/root/language_review_a":null,"/root/language_review_b":"13 October 2026"},"reviewType":"independent-adversarial-model-review","humanReview":false}},{"id":"adv-souda-hearsay","title":"そうだ : rapporter une information","domain":"grammar","level":"N4","levelBasis":"Editorial difficulty estimate; not an official JLPT item assignment","taxonomy":"evidence","aliases":["souda-hearsay","そうだ"],"explanationFr":"Forme neutre complète + そうだ rapporte une information entendue ou lue. Contrairement à l’apparence, on conserve la terminaison de l’adjectif et だ après un no