é un nom (13 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N3 ; statut : editorial-draft. (13 October 2026)\n\nEnlever い d’un adjectif en い, ou な d’un adjectif en な, puis ajouter さ. いい utilise la base よい et donne よさ. Le nom exprime une qualité ou son degré. (13 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| この部屋の広さに驚きました。 (このへやのひろさにおどろきました。) | La taille de cette pièce m’a surpris. (13 October 2026) |\n| 静かさが好きです。 (しずかさがすきです。) | J’aime le calme. (13 October 2026) |\n| 日本語の面白さが分かってきました。 (にほんごのおもしろさがわかってきました。) | Je commence à comprendre ce qui fait l’intérêt du japonais. (13 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-verb-groups, grammar-copula, grammar-i-adjectives. (13 October 2026)\n\n- [Adjective Nominalization I: ～さ & ～み](https://imabi.org/adjective-nominalization/) ; Seth Coonrod, original IMABI curriculum author ; Copyright retained by author; no open license verified ; vérifié : 12 October 2026. (13 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"a71c77f0866a93062dd0bb2642208442b2c1b9f8f9c1c849ef839460110aef54","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"a71c77f0866a93062dd0bb2642208442b2c1b9f8f9c1c849ef839460110aef54","reviewerIds":["/root/language_review_a","/root/language_review_b"],"evidenceUrls":["https://imabi.org/adjective-nominalization/","https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/030.html"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtByReviewer":{"/root/language_review_a":null,"/root/language_review_b":"13 October 2026"},"reviewType":"independent-adversarial-model-review","humanReview":false}},{"id":"adv-me","title":"め : un degré légèrement orienté","domain":"grammar","level":"N3","levelBasis":"Editorial difficulty estimate; not an official JLPT item assignment","taxonomy":"word-formation","aliases":["me","め"],"explanationFr":"Après certaines bases adjectivales, め indique un degré un peu plus marqué dans la direction choisie: 早め, 大きめ. Les mots attestés guident l’usage.","contra