rd":65,"revisionDate":"14 October 2026","markdown":"## expand-copula-past : でした : situer une phrase nominale dans le passé (14 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N5 ; statut : editorial-draft. (14 October 2026)\n\nDans le registre poli, Nでした situe l'identification dans le passé ; Nではありませんでした la nie dans le passé. Le temps concerne l'énoncé, pas le nom lui-même. (14 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| 昨日は休みでした。 (きのうはやすみでした。) | Hier, c'était un jour de repos. (14 October 2026) |\n| 昨日は休みではありませんでした。 (きのうはやすみではありませんでした。) | Hier, ce n'était pas un jour de repos. (14 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-copula. (14 October 2026)\n\n- [TUFS Japanese grammar module 004](https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/004.html) ; Tokyo University of Foreign Studies ; Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified ; vérifié : 14 October 2026. (14 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"27cd9ed20874462017bae6581b9238ecb4577426409fbce7344329cf835c125b","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"27cd9ed20874462017bae6581b9238ecb4577426409fbce7344329cf835c125b","reviewerIds":["/root/expansion_review_first","/root/expansion_review_second"],"evidenceUrls":["https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/004.html"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtByReviewer":{"/root/expansion_review_first":"14 October 2026","/root/expansion_review_second":"14 October 2026"},"reviewType":"independent-adversarial-model-review","humanReview":false}},{"id":"expand-location-existence","title":"場所に : placer ce qui existe","domain":"grammar","level":"N5","levelBasis":"Local editorial estimate; not an official JLPT item allocation","aliases":["場所に","location-existence"],"explanationFr":"Dans 場所にNがあります／います, に situe la chose ou l'être dont on affirme l'existence. Pour une activité effectuée quelque part, le lieu se marque normalement avec で.","frenchLearnerTrap":"庭で猫がいます ne constitue pas la construction ordinaire pour dire qu'un chat se trouve dans le jardin.","examples":[{"ja":"部屋に机があります。","reading":"へやにつくえがあります。","fr":"Il y a un bureau dans la pièce.","origin":"Original example; independent adversarial review pending"},{"ja":"公園に犬がいます。","reading":"こうえんにいぬがいます。","fr":"Il y a un chien dans le parc.","origin":"Original example; independent adversarial review pending"}],"prerequisites":["grammar-copula","grammar-existence"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/006.html","title":"TUFS Japanese grammar module 006","publisher":"Tokyo University of Foreign Studies","checkedAt":"14 October 2026","license":"Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified","reuse":"Link and original concise explanation/examples only; no publisher lesson or audio reproduced"}],"status":"editorial-draft","reviewScope":"Source available; content alignment, kana and translations await independent reviews","createdAt":"14 October 2026","learnerState":"not-assessed","oralPromptsFr":["Il y a un bureau dans la pièce.","Il y a un chien dans le parc."],"levelEstimated":true,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/language/LanguageExpansionRecords.json","corpus":"language","recordShard":234,"revisionDate":"14 October 2026","markdown":"## expand-location-existence : 場所に : placer ce qui existe (14 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N5 ; statut : editorial-draft. (14 October 2026)\n\nDans 場所にNがあります／います, に situe la chose ou l'être dont on affirme l'existence. Pour une activité effectuée quelque part, le lieu se marque normalement avec で. (14 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| 部屋に机があります。 (へやにつくえがあります。) | Il y a un bureau dans la pièce. (14 October 2026) |\n| 公園に犬がいます。 (こうえんにいぬがいます。) | Il y a un chien dans le parc. (14 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-copula, grammar-existence. (14 October 2026)\n\n- [TUFS Japanese grammar module 006](https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/006.html) ; Tokyo University of Foreign Studies ; Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified ; vérifié : 14 October 2026. (14 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"29fbdae36970ff36e88f0b51ebdc967951ee9df548d749e2cbd6ee6a19990690","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"29fbdae36970ff36e88f0b51ebdc967951ee9df548d749e2cbd6ee6a19990690","reviewerIds":["/root/expansion_review_first","/root/expansion_review_second"],"evidenceUrls":["https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/006.html"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtByReviewer":{"/root/expansion_review_first":"14 October 2026","/root/expansion_review_second":"14 October 2026"},"reviewType":"independent-adversarial-model-review","humanReview":false}},{"id":"expand-spatial-nouns","title":"上・下・中 : situer par rapport à un objet","domain":"grammar","level":"N5","levelBasis":"Local editorial estimate; not an official JLPT item allocation","aliases":["上・下・中","spatial-nouns"],"explanationFr":"Un nom de repère suivi de の et d'un nom spatial forme un groupe comme 机の上, le dessus du bureau. Ce groupe peut recevoir に dans une phrase d'existence.","frenchLearnerTrap":"の lie le repère au nom spatial ; il ne remplace pas le に final du lieu d'existence.","examples":[{"ja":"机の上に本があります。","reading":"つくえのうえにほんがあります。","fr":"Il y a un livre sur le bureau.","origin":"Original example; independent adversarial review pending"},{"ja":"箱の中に鍵があります。","reading":"はこのなかにかぎがあります。","fr":"Il y a une clé dans la boîte.","origin":"Original example; independent adversarial review pending"}],"prerequisites":["grammar-copula","expand-noun-no","expand-location-existence"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/007.html","title":"TUFS Japanese grammar module 007","publisher":"Tokyo University of Foreign Studies","checkedAt":"14 October 2026","license":"Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified","reuse":"Link and original concise explanation/examples only; no publisher lesson or audio reproduced"}],"status":"editorial-draft","reviewScope":"Source available; content alignment, kana and translations await independent reviews","createdAt":"14 October 2026","learnerState":"not-assessed","oralPromptsFr":["Il y a un livre sur le bureau.","Il y a une clé dans la boîte."],"levelEstimated":true,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/language/LanguageExpansionRecords.json","corpus":"language","recordShard":248,"revisionDate":"14 October 2026","markdown":"## expand-spatial-nouns : 上・下・中 : situer par rapport à un objet (14 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N5 ; statut : editorial-draft. (14 October 2026)\n\nUn nom de repère suivi de の et d'un nom spatial forme un groupe comme 机の上, le dessus du bureau. Ce groupe peut recevoir に dans une phrase d'existence. (14 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| 机の上に本があります。 (つくえのうえにほんがあります。) | Il y a un livre sur le bureau. (14 October 2026) |\n| 箱の中に鍵があります。 (はこのなかにかぎがあります。) | Il y a une clé dans la boîte. (14 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-copula, expand-noun-no, expand-location-existence. (14 October 2026)\n\n- [TUFS Japanese grammar module 007](https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/007.html) ; Tokyo University of Foreign Studies ; Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified ; vérifié : 14 October 2026. (14 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"8be6e25262665ad1550f11dad2c79b51bb5853f9e57a293336511208b1130722","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"8be6e25262665ad1550f11dad2c79b51bb5853f9e57a293336511208b1130722","reviewerIds":["/root/expansion_review_first","/root/expansion_review_second"],"evidenceUrls":["https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/007.html"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtB