 (14 October 2026)\n\nの relie un nom déterminant à un nom déterminé. La relation dépend du contexte : appartenance, origine ou association, et ne se réduit pas au possessif français. (14 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| これは私の本です。 (これはわたしのほんです。) | Ceci est mon livre. (14 October 2026) |\n| 日本語の本を読みます。 (にほんごのほんをよみます。) | Je lis un livre de japonais. (14 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-copula, grammar-polite-nonpast. (14 October 2026)\n\n- [TUFS Japanese grammar module 008](https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/008.html) ; Tokyo University of Foreign Studies ; Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified ; vérifié : 14 October 2026. (14 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"c24d98aea88f1d516f81f5a894917d09f1eb1b9e2078849bc893a11662be17f2","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"c24d98aea88f1d516f81f5a894917d09f1eb1b9e2078849bc893a11662be17f2","reviewerIds":["/root/expansion_review_first","/root/expansion_review_second"],"evidenceUrls":["https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/008.html"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtByReviewer":{"/root/expansion_review_first":"14 October 2026","/root/expansion_review_second":"14 October 2026"},"reviewType":"independent-adversarial-model-review","humanReview":false}},{"id":"expand-i-adjective-noun","title":"AいN : qualifier directement un nom","domain":"grammar","level":"N5","levelBasis":"Local editorial estimate; not an official JLPT item allocation","aliases":["AいN","i-adjective-noun"],"explanationFr":"Un adjectif en い dans sa forme affirmative non passée précède directement le nom qu'il qualifie. La politesse se marque à la fin de la phrase, pas en insérant です entre l'adjectif et le nom.","frenchLearnerTrap":"高い店 se construit sans な ; 高いな店 n'est pas la construction étudiée.","examples":[{"ja":"新しい靴を買いました。","reading":"あたらしいくつをかいました。","fr":"J'ai acheté des chaussures neuves.","origin":"Original example; independent adversarial review pending"},{"ja":"小さい店があります。","reading":"ちいさいみせがあります。","fr":"Il y a une petite boutique.","origin":"Original example; independent adversarial review pending"}],"prerequisites":["grammar-copula","grammar-i-adjectives","expand-polite-verb-past"],"sources":[{"url":"https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/009.html","title":"TUFS Japanese grammar module 009","publisher":"Tokyo University of Foreign Studies","checkedAt":"14 October 2026","license":"Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified","reuse":"Link and original concise explanation/examples only; no publisher lesson or audio reproduced"}],"status":"editorial-draft","reviewScope":"Source available; content alignment, kana and translations await independent reviews","createdAt":"14 October 2026","learnerState":"not-assessed","oralPromptsFr":["J'ai acheté des chaussures neuves.","Il y a une petite boutique."],"levelEstimated":true,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/language/LanguageExpansionRecords.json","corpus":"language","recordShard":140,"revisionDate":"14 October 2026","markdown":"## expand-i-adjective-noun : AいN : qualifier directement un nom (14 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N5 ; statut : editorial-draft. (14 October 2026)\n\nUn adjectif en い dans sa forme affirmative non passée précède directement le nom qu'il qualifie. La politesse se marque à la fin de la phrase, pas en insérant です entre l'adjectif et le nom. (14 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| 新しい靴を買いました。 (あたらしいくつをかいました。) | J'ai acheté des chaussures neuves. (14 October 2026) |\n| 小さい店があります。 (ちいさいみせがあります。) | Il y a une petite boutique. (14 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-copula, grammar-i-adjectives, expand-polite-verb-past. (14 October 2026)\n\n- [TUFS Japanese grammar module 009](https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/009.html) ; Tokyo University o