ified","reuse":"Link and original concise explanation/examples only; no publisher lesson or audio reproduced"}],"status":"editorial-draft","reviewScope":"Source available; content alignment, kana and translations await independent reviews","createdAt":"14 October 2026","learnerState":"not-assessed","oralPromptsFr":["J'ai pris le petit-déjeuner.","Hier, je n'ai pas travaillé."],"levelEstimated":true,"origin":"/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-japanese/research/language/LanguageExpansionRecords.json","corpus":"language","recordShard":236,"revisionDate":"14 October 2026","markdown":"## expand-polite-verb-past : ました・ませんでした : le passé poli (14 October 2026)\n\nDomaine : grammar ; niveau : N5 ; statut : editorial-draft. (14 October 2026)\n\nLa terminaison ました indique un événement ou état passé ; ませんでした le nie. On la construit à partir de la même base que ます, sans ajouter です. (14 October 2026)\n\n| Japonais et lecture | Français |\n|---|---|\n| 朝ご飯を食べました。 (あさごはんをたべました。) | J'ai pris le petit-déjeuner. (14 October 2026) |\n| 昨日は働きませんでした。 (きのうははたらきませんでした。) | Hier, je n'ai pas travaillé. (14 October 2026) |\n\nPrérequis : grammar-copula, grammar-polite-nonpast. (14 October 2026)\n\n- [TUFS Japanese grammar module 025](https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/025.html) ; Tokyo University of Foreign Studies ; Copyright retained by publisher; no open licence verified ; vérifié : 14 October 2026. (14 October 2026)\n","lessonContentVersion":"1","lessonContentHash":"705e36e8b658e5de973c36506daccfc668902a3730ec1929d584888a2ff9e587","lessonValidation":{"status":"approved","contentVersion":"1","contentHash":"705e36e8b658e5de973c36506daccfc668902a3730ec1929d584888a2ff9e587","reviewerIds":["/root/expansion_review_first","/root/expansion_review_second"],"evidenceUrls":["https://www.coelang.tufs.ac.jp/mt/ja/gmod/contents/explanation/025.html"],"unresolvedFindings":[],"reviewedAtByReviewer":{"/root/expansion_review_first":"14 October 2026","/root/expansion_review_se